===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|gestalten}}

# A [[collection]] of [[physical]], [[biological]], [[psychological]] or [[symbolic]] [[element]]s that creates a [[whole]], [[unified]] [[concept]] or [[pattern]] which is [[other]] than the [[sum]] of its [[part]]s due to the relationships between the parts (of a [[character]], [[personality]], [[entity]], or [[being]]).
#: {{ux|en|This biography is the first one to consider fully the writer's '''gestalt'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Mary did not approve of the Eleanor '''gestalt'''. "I been to Woonsocket S.D., Eleanor McGovern's hometown," she said, "and nobody there? I mean nobody? dresses like that."|author=John L. Hess; Karen Hess|title=The Taste of America|publisher=Grossman|location=New York|year=1977}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=w:Metaphors We Live By|author=w:George Lakoff; {{w|Mark Johnson (philosopher)|Mark Johnson}}|year=1980|chapter=15|passage=Thus one activity, talking, is understood in terms of another, physical fighting. Structuring our experience in terms of such multidimensional '''gestalts''' is what makes our experience coherent.}}
#* {{quote-book|en||year=1996|passage={{...}} depending on the kinds of speech children hear directed to them, they may first learn unanalyzed "'''gestalts'''" (e.g., social expressions like "What's that?" uttered as a single unit) instead of learning single words that are then freely recombined {{...}}|author=Kathy Hirsh-Pasek|title=The Origins of Grammar|publisher=The MIT Press|location=Cambridge, MA}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|passage=So different were our appearances and approaches and general '''gestalts''' that we had something of an epic rivalry from '74 through '77.|author=w:David Foster Wallace|title=A Supposedly Fun Thing I'll Never Do Again|location=Boston|publisher=Little, Brown and Co.|edition=1st Back Bay}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=August 2003|passage=The clusters of behavioral '''gestalten'''... the probability factors... the subtypes of crimes... the constellations of criminal subtypes...|author=Jay Kirk|title=Watching the Detectives|magazine=Harpers Magazine|volume=307|issue=1839|page=61|url=https://harpers.org/archive/2003/08/watching-the-detectives/}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Jonathan Nasaw|title=Fear Itself|passage=Obviously it was related to the entire '''gestalt''' of Simon's polyphobia and compensatory counterphobia. The boys used to watch horror movies on late-night television {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|date=2025-03-06|author=Sheryl Gay Stolberg|quotee=w:Bill Cassidy|title=A Skeptical G.O.P. Senator Makes His Peace With Kennedy|work=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/05/us/politics/bill-cassidy-rfk-measles.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=“He [Robert F. Kennedy Jr.] also said, ‘We’re making vaccinations available. We’re doing this for vaccination. We’re doing that for vaccination.’ So if you take the '''gestalt''' of it, the '''gestalt''' was, ‘Let’s get vaccinated!’”}}

